Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE (@pe-motors-sourcebook: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR
U.S. Department of Energy. Improving Motor and Drive System Performance: A Sourcebook for Industry, second edition, February 2014. [Official complete sourcebook](https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2014/04/f15/amo_motors_sourcebook_web.pdf) · [DOE motor-system resources](https://www.energy.gov/cmei/ito/motor-systems).

Read the whole sourcebook: system basics, performance opportunities, operating conditions, selection, adjustable-speed drives, distribution/power quality, maintenance/service-centre evaluation and system economics. Relate motor efficiency to the actual driven load and operating schedule rather than comparing only nameplate peak efficiency.

The source explicitly describes practical opportunities rather than a comprehensive machine-theory textbook. Edition/date and full scope were checked through primary publisher material on 29 October 2026. Its NEMA table excerpts and historical minimum-efficiency references retain their own dates/rights; they are not current compliance tables for every jurisdiction. Use the graduate machine reading for design theory and actual current manufacturer/authority data for an application. No book, tables or software are copied here.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
